 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 535683,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b991d7289cd014dd.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Silva, Paula et al./Semantic Scholar)\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The table shows the results of the two-point discrimination test for a population.</p>\n<p>In the test, two sharp points, such as two thumbtacks, are brought into contact with the subject’s skin. The subject reports if he or she feels one point or two points. The test can be used to determine the density of receptors in skin.</p>\n<p>What is a conclusion that can be made based on this data?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1049023,
     "content_html": "The highest concentration of mechanoreceptors are in the lower arm."
    },
    {
     "id": 1049024,
     "content_html": "The upper arm has a higher density of receptors than the lower arm."
    },
    {
     "id": 1049025,
     "content_html": "The long and little fingers have the highest concentration of receptors."
    },
    {
     "id": 1049026,
     "content_html": "There are no mechanoreceptors in the fingers other than the thumb, the long finger and the little finger."
    }
   ],
